WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:07.140 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Music]  rockstar has released a meaty six-minute  gameplay trailer for Red Dead Redemption  - there's a lot to unpack here like the  gorgeous open world impressive attention  to detail and some of the various new  mechanics however I'm most curious about  how the player will interact with the  world based on the gameplay trailer  Rockstar is trying to change it up  partially through NPC interactions and  the video the narrator says your guns  aren't the only way to interact with the  environment this may seem small compared  to everything else the trailer shows but  if done correctly this has the potential  to shake up the open-world formula  [Music]  for the longest time especially in  sandbox action games like GTA and  assassin's creed non-player characters  apart from being set dressings seem to  have two responses to the player  friendly or violent if they are friendly  they will either stay out of your way or  offer you a mission and if they are  agitated they will probably try to kill  you today these binary NPC responses  have gotten predictable if you see some  people with guns or swords drawn it  probably means you should ready yourself  up for a fight in the video Rockstar  claims that you will be able to  contextually defuse or escalate  confrontations threaten witnesses and  reason with a town sheriff this could  make every random interaction or  encounter feel dynamic and carry more  consequences picture this you ride into  a small dusty town you are low on  resources and money so you decide to rob  a warehouse while rummaging through the  stuff in the building the owner walks in  and spots you without skipping a beat he  runs for the town sheriff you can stop  him before he gets to the sheriff by  putting a bullet in his back or tackling  him to the ground and threatening him or  maybe you're too slow and before you can  catch him he's already informed the  sheriff the sheriff confronts you do you  retaliate and kill the sheriff knowing  that the whole town could erupt in  gunfire or do you back down although  this is a hypothetical situation this  level of interaction has a ton of  potential and it begs the question what  type of outlaw will you be once and for  all we don't know much about Arthur  Morgan's character arc but this system  gives the player the potential to shape  who Arthur Morgan is you could be a cold  unforgiving outlaw or a cunning cowboy  with a silver tongue Rockstar hasn't  talked about whether or not your actions  will have far-reaching consequences but  giving the player the freedom to react  to these situations as they see fit is  enticing you aren't locked into a  firefight just because you picked a  fight with a bar patron or trampled  someone with a horse  speaking of your horse these dynamic  interactions will extend to your steed  different breeds will have different  attributes and personalities some breeds  may not do well with water while others  might scare easily you can grow your  bond with your horse by feeding it  grooming it and calming it they're  stronger the bond with your horse is the  easier it will be to calm once again  this may seem small but it could add  another level of depth and believability  to the world characters and animals you  come across seem like more than just set  dressing you can trick them threaten  them agitate them and react to them as  you please it's hard to say just how  in-depth this feature will be when the  game releases on October 26th but we'll  be sure to let you know if we find out  more  [Music]

